+The built-in `codex` profile (`dokimi/repos/profiles/codex.yaml`) runs
+`codex exec` non-interactively: `--model {model}`, `--ephemeral`, the prompt
+after `--`, `CODEX_HOME` as the per-run config directory and the `text` trace
+(stdout is the final message). Codex has no flag to switch tools off or to cap
+turns or spend, so `none` and `read` both select `--sandbox read-only`,
+`{max_turns}` and `{budget}` are not passed, and the timeout bounds a run. It
+declares `AGENTS.md` (and `AGENTS.override.md`) from the git root down to the
+working directory, and no `bridge`: Codex does not read `CLAUDE.md`.
+
